  reel_script says the leaf roller infestation is in the Krishnarayapuram area, but the article only says the Karur district Agriculture department issued the advisory; the Krishnarayapuram dateline is not tied to the infestation itself
  reel_script and caption say the spray can be used 'when attack is low or absent' - the article says the neem/azadirachtin spray is to be used when attack is low OR even when there is no attack; this is consistent, but reel_script phrasing 'தாக்குதல் குறைவாக இருந்தாலும், தாக்குதல் இல்லாவிட்டாலும்' omits the 'ஓட்டும் திரவம்' context - minor
  reel_script states the Karur district Agriculture department's advisory explicitly; slides_spec slide 'தாக்குதல் குறைவு' says 'மருந்து தெளிக்கலாம்' while the article says the spray is recommended under low/no attack - acceptable
  caption and reel_script say the 100-leaf threshold means 'when 10 of 100 leaves are affected', but the Tamil wording '100 இலைக்கு 10 இலைக்கு மேல்' is grammatically awkward and does not clearly convey 'more than 10 affected leaves per 100', creating an unclear sentence
  reel_script says 'ஷாம்பு 3 பாக்கெட் கலந்து தெளிக்கலாம்' and 'திரவம் கலந்து' conflates the shampoo with the spray mixing instruction, which is not clearly separated from the chemical instructions as in the article
  slides_spec 'தாக்குதல் அதிகம்' slide describes chlorpyrifos treatment as applicable only when 'தாக்குதல் அதிகம்', but the article gives the threshold as 10 of 100 leaves, and the slide heading 'தாக்குதல் அதிகம்' is an added characterization not in the article
  slides_spec line 'கூடுதல் செலவு குறையும்' is attached to the chlorpyrifos sentence, mixing two facts (pest control and cost reduction) into one line
  reel_script 'விவசாயிகளின் கூடுதல் செலவு குறையும்' and 'மகசூல் அதிகரிக்கும்' are presented as certain outcomes; article only says cost reduction 'can be' achieved and yield can be taken, a modest overstatement
